// TaskForest Windows resource script.
//
// Embeds the app icon as the executable's PRIMARY icon at resource id 1.
// gpui 0.2.2's Windows backend (platform/windows/platform.rs `load_icon`) calls
// LoadImageW(exe_module, MAKEINTRESOURCE(1), IMAGE_ICON, ...) and installs the
// result as the window-class `hIcon` — i.e. the taskbar / alt-tab / titlebar
// icon. Windows Explorer independently shows the LOWEST-id icon for the .exe
// file itself. So a single resource at id 1 satisfies both gpui's window icon
// and the Explorer file icon.
//
// This is a different resource TYPE (RT_ICON = 1 / RT_GROUP_ICON = 14) from
// gpui's `windows-manifest` feature (RT_MANIFEST = 24, also at id 1) — resource
// ids are namespaced per-type, so the two id-1 resources coexist without a
// duplicate-resource link error.
//
// The ICON path is relative to this .rc file's directory, so taskmanager.ico
// sits next to it under packaging/windows/.
1 ICON "taskmanager.ico"
